{"text":"MODEL_FEEDBACK_JSON:
{
  "positive_alignment_reasons": [
    "Aenima and Lateralus feel like natural next choices after 10.000 Days because I want more of Tool's intricate rhythms and immersive, heavy songs.",
    "The War Within connects with my interest in Advance And Vanquish and In Flames through aggressive guitar riffs, while the melodic rock choices reflect another part of my listening history."
  ],
  "negative_misalignment_reasons": [
    "Year Zero and Portrait Of An American Family miss what I want today because electronic and industrial textures do not satisfy my current interest in guitar-driven heaviness.",
    "Daughtry and Fallen appeal to me, but their accessible or melodic sound makes them less urgent choices than Tool's complexity or The War Within's aggression."
  ],
  "overgeneralized_signals": [
    "Darkness and aggression seem to be treated as enough to connect albums, even though industrial rock and riff-driven metal appeal to me differently.",
    "My past interest in accessible rock seems to carry too much weight for what I want to hear right now."
  ],
  "missing_or_underweighted_signals": [
    "My latest choice, 10.000 Days, makes exploring more Tool especially appealing right now.",
    "I am choosing selectively: complex rhythms and strong metal riffs matter more today than a broad resemblance to rock albums I have explored before."
  ],
  "summary_diagnosis": "The recommendations recognize my interest in heavy rock, but sometimes overlook the specific rhythms, guitar sound, and immediate pull of exploring more Tool."
}"}
